  "interpretation": {
    "primary_finding": "The full live LLM agentic run is operationally robust but substantially weaker than the deterministic source-derived S5/S6 control. The gap is caused mainly by live extractor recall and precision, not by runtime failures.",
    "critic_effect": "The S6 critic/refiner layer removes 50 facts, raising precision from 0.5047 to 0.5299 but lowering recall from 0.4199 to 0.3997, leaving F1 essentially unchanged.",
    "refiner_effect": "The refiner triggered safety fallback on 96 of 100 records, so current S6 quality should be attributed mostly to deterministic validation plus critic filtering, not to successful LLM rewriting.",
    "thesis_claim": "Use the full run as negative/diagnostic SOTA-comparison evidence: multi-agent orchestration and hard gates are executable and auditable, but unconstrained live LLM extraction does not beat a domain-specific deterministic extractor for semi-structured ATCSCC advisories."
  }
